import AxQM.Postulates.API.FourGateReachableTowerDensity
import AxQM.Postulates.API.RzThreeFifthsMeasurement
import AxQM.Core.FourGateNamedTower

/-!
# Named four-gate tower density + the four-gate measurement realisation of `R_z(θ)`
(N&C Exercise 4.43, four-gate bridge — density core + the Exercise-4.41 grounded realisation)

The grounded tower operator density
`exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions`
(`AxQM/Postulates/API/FourGateReachableTowerDensity.lean`) states that, up to a global phase,
every tower evolution `T : Evolution (qtower n qubit)` is a limit of the operators of the grounded
reachable tower circuit submonoid `reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ`. The named-gate assembly
`AxQM/Core/FourGateNamedTower.lean` re-expressed that whole submonoid over the four *named* gates:

  `reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions n θ ≤ namedFourGateTowerGates n θ`

(`reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions_le_namedFourGateTowerGates`), where `namedFourGateTowerGates n θ`
is generated by the tower-wire placements of `hadamardGate, sGate, cnotGate, toffoliGate` together
with the base rotation `rotZGate θ`.

## Two results

The full Exercise-4.43 claim is that `H, S, CNOT, Toffoli` **with measurement** are universal: the
four *unitary* gates alone generate the *discrete* Clifford + Toffoli group, and the irrational
rotation `R_z(θ)` (`cos θ = 3/5`, `θ/2π` irrational — Exercises 4.41/4.42) is not among them; it is
supplied by a **measurement** of the four-gate circuit. This file proves two results:

* `exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_namedFourGateTowerGates` — **the density core.** With
  `R_z(θ)` available as a generator, the four-gate model is dense. On its own this carries
  `rotZGate θ` as a **free** generator, so it is not Exercise 4.43's four-gate claim.
* `rzThreeFifthsMeasurement_success_realizes_rotZ` — **the four-gate measurement realisation.**
  The Figure-4.17 circuit `rzThreeFifthsCircuit` (built from `H, S, Toffoli` on two ancillas +
  target), followed by the two-ancilla measurement `rzTwoAncillaMeasurement`, realises
  `R_z(rzThreeFifthsAngle)` on the target on its success outcome `(0, 0)` (probability
  `‖c‖² = 5/8`) (Exercise 4.41).

**These two are not integrated.** The density (first) treats `rotZGate θ` as a free unitary
generator; the realisation (second) shows `R_z(θ)` is a four-gate + measurement construction.
Fusing them into a single "four-gate circuits *with post-selected measurement* are dense"
statement needs a formal *reachable-with-measurement* notion (a measurement-realised generator
inside the universality submonoid), which the unitary-`Evolution`-submonoid framework here does
not provide. The statement of Exercise 4.43 is in `AxQM/NC/Ch4/Exercise4_43.lean`.

The statements use `.op`/`.vec` and `closure`; the realisation uses `rzTwoAncillaMeasurement` and
the four-gate circuit `rzThreeFifthsCircuit` (`AxQM/Postulates/API/RzThreeFifthsMeasurement.lean` /
`AxQM/Postulates/API/RzThreeFifthsCircuit.lean`). The named submonoid `namedFourGateTowerGates`
and the containment it consumes are in `AxQM/Core/FourGateNamedTower.lean`.
-/

namespace AxQM

noncomputable section

/-- **The named four-gate tower density core** (any `θ` with `cos θ = 3/5`). For *any* tower
evolution `T : Evolution (qtower n qubit)`, some global phase `e^{iα}` makes

  `e^{iα} • T.op ∈ closure ((·.op) '' namedFourGateTowerGates n θ)`,

so every unitary on the `(n+1)`-qubit control tower is, up to an (unobservable) global phase, a
limit of the operators of circuits drawn from `namedFourGateTowerGates n θ` — the submonoid
generated by the tower-wire placements of the four named gates `hadamardGate, sGate, cnotGate,
toffoliGate` together with the base rotation `rotZGate θ`.

This is the reusable analytic core: it holds for an abstract `θ` and treats `rotZGate θ` as a
**free** generator, so on its own it is **not** Exercise 4.43's four-gate universality (which
requires `R_z(θ)` to be *supplied by the four gates + measurement*, not posited — see
`rzThreeFifthsMeasurement_success_realizes_rotZ` for the realisation, and
`AxQM/NC/Ch4/Exercise4_43.lean` for the statement).

Immediate from the grounded tower operator density
`exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions`: the containment
`reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions_le_namedFourGateTowerGates` (every grounded reachable tower circuit
is a named four-gate circuit) includes the grounded operator image into the named one
(`SetLike.coe_subset_coe` + `Set.image_mono`), and `closure_mono` carries the phase-shifted operator
across. -/
theorem exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_namedFourGateTowerGates {n : ℕ} {θ : ℝ}
    (hθ : Real.cos θ = 3 / 5) (T : Evolution (qtower n qubit)) :
    ∃ α : ℝ, Complex.exp ((α : ℂ) * Complex.I) • T.op ∈
      closure ((fun E : Evolution (qtower n qubit) => E.op) ''
        (namedFourGateTowerGates n θ : Set (Evolution (qtower n qubit)))) := by
  obtain ⟨α, hα⟩ := exists_phase_smul_op_mem_closure_op_reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions hθ T
  exact ⟨α, closure_mono (Set.image_mono
    (SetLike.coe_subset_coe.2 (reachableTowerCircuitEvolutions_le_namedFourGateTowerGates n θ))) hα⟩

/-- **The four-gate circuit realises `R_z(θ)` by measurement** (Exercise 4.41, `cos θ = 3/5`). The
base rotation `rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle` — the sole non-`{H, S, CNOT, Toffoli}` generator of
`namedFourGateTowerGates n rzThreeFifthsAngle` — is *not* a fifth gate but a four-gate +
measurement construction, established here using the four-gate circuit `rzThreeFifthsCircuit` and
the measurement `rzTwoAncillaMeasurement`:

1. **The measurement success operator**
   (`rzTwoAncillaMeasurement_op_rzThreeFifthsCircuit_qubitBasis`): applying the success-outcome
   `(0, 0)` operator of the two-ancilla measurement `rzTwoAncillaMeasurement` to the output of the
   Figure-4.17 circuit `rzThreeFifthsCircuit` (`H, S, Toffoli` on two ancillas + target) on
   `|0, 0, t⟩` collapses it to `rzThreeFifthsAmp 0 0 t • |0, 0, t⟩`.
2. **The success amplitude is `R_z(θ)`** (`rzThreeFifthsCircuit_success_eq_rotZ`): there is a scalar
   `c` with `‖c‖² = 5/8` (the input-independent success probability) such that
   `rzThreeFifthsAmp 0 0 t • |t⟩ = c • (rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle).op |t⟩` on the target.

Composed, the four gates and one measurement apply `R_z(rzThreeFifthsAngle)` to the target on the
`(0, 0)` outcome — the Exercise-4.41 realisation. This realises the `rotZGate` generator of the
density core in `{H, S, CNOT, Toffoli}` + measurement; integrating this realisation into the
density statement (so the density no longer posits `rotZGate` freely) is not done here. -/
theorem rzThreeFifthsMeasurement_success_realizes_rotZ :
    (∀ t : Fin 2,
        (rzTwoAncillaMeasurement.op (0, 0))
            (rzThreeFifthsCircuit.evolvePure
              ((qubitBasis 0).tmul ((qubitBasis 0).tmul (qubitBasis t)))).vec
          = rzThreeFifthsAmp 0 0 t •
              ((qubitBasis 0).tmul ((qubitBasis 0).tmul (qubitBasis t))).vec) ∧
      ∃ c : ℂ, ‖c‖ ^ 2 = 5 / 8 ∧ ∀ t : Fin 2,
        rzThreeFifthsAmp 0 0 t • (qubitBasis t).vec
          = c • (rotZGate rzThreeFifthsAngle).op (qubitBasis t).vec :=
  ⟨rzTwoAncillaMeasurement_op_rzThreeFifthsCircuit_qubitBasis, rzThreeFifthsCircuit_success_eq_rotZ⟩

end

end AxQM
